      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve \\(2.4 \\times 0.2\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the decimals to fractions:**\n   - \\(2.4\\) can be written as \\(\\frac{24}{10}\\).\n   - \\(0.2\\) can be written as \\(\\frac{2}{10}\\).\n\n2. **Multiply the fractions:**\n   \\[\n   2.4 \\times 0.2 = \\frac{24}{10} \\times \\frac{2}{10}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply the numerators and the denominators:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{24 \\times 2}{10 \\times 10} = \\frac{48}{100}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the fraction:**\n   - The greatest common divisor (GCD) of 48 and 100 is 4.\n   - Divide both the numerator and the denominator by 4:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{48 \\div 4}{100 \\div 4} = \\frac{12}{25}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Convert the simplified fraction back to a decimal:**\n   - To convert \\(\\frac{12}{25}\\) to a decimal, perform the division \\(12 \\div 25\\):\n   \\[\n   12 \\div 25 = 0.48\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.48}\n\\]",
